d was the subject of a cholera study in 2023, indicating potential public health challenges. The Souari Chiefdom (traditional chieftaincy) is listed as a tourist attraction. Historic neighborhoods may feature aging infrastructure and higher population density, increasing their vulnerability to health and security risks.	Located in the urban core of Garoua. Accessible via urban roads and motorbike taxis.	Historic neighborhood with an established but potentially aging real estate stock. Moderate rents. Traditional land tenure systems may complicate formal transactions.	Historic Fulani/Peul community. The presence of a traditional chiefdom (Souari Chiefdom) reflects a long-standing and well-established community structure.	Souari is one of Garoua’s historic neighborhoods, cited alongside Yelwa, Roumde-Adjia, Foulbere, and Lopere. It hosts a traditional chiefdom (Souari Chiefdom) and includes the secondary zone of Souari Depot, which has experienced public health issues, including cholera cases.	["Historic neighborhood with traditional chieftaincy (Souari Chieftaincy). Local markets and basic services. A cholera risk has been documented (2023 KAP study in Souari Depot)."]	["Souari Chiefdom (traditional chieftaincy/palace), adjacent neighborhood of Souari Depot (site of a cholera study)."]	["Cholera and public health risks (documented outbreak in 2023 at the Souari depot), dense historic urban fabric, general security risks in the North Region."]
